:Require file://mu.apln
:Namespace SQEN

⎕IO←0

opsys←{⍵⊃⍨'Win' 'Lin' 'Mac'⍳⊂3↑⊃'.'⎕WG'APLVersion'}
mu←#.mu
fenster←mu.fenster_dll←opsys 'fenster.dll' 'fenster.so' 'fenster.dylib'

⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝
⍝ Sequence Enumeration Exercise! ⍝
⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝

⍝ You are designing an alarm system and it is your job to make sure that the 
⍝ alarm behaves the way that it should. Here are the system requirements:
⍝ 
⍝ 1  The security alarm has a detector that sends a trip signal when motion is 
⍝    detected.
⍝ 2  The security alarm is activated by pressing the Set button.
⍝ 3  The Set button is illuminated when the security alarm is set.
⍝ 4  If a trip signal occurs while the security alarm is set, a high pitched tone 
⍝    (alarm) is emitted.
⍝ 5  A three-digit code must be entered to turn off the alarm tone.
⍝ 6  Correct entry of the code deactivates the security alarm.
⍝ 7  If a mistake is made when entering the code, the user must press the Clear 
⍝    button before the code can be reentered. 
⍝ 
⍝ Your alarm system has a light on it and an alarm that can sound. You need to 
⍝ make sure that the alarm is sounding at the right times and that the light 
⍝ properly indicates when the system is armed or when it is disarmed. In this 
⍝ case, your system expects to see whether the system is armed or not by the 
⍝ Boolean variable `light`, and whether the alarm is on or off by the Boolean 
⍝ variable `alarm`. 

alarm←0
light←0

⍝ We've done some of the hard work for you already by defining a set of input 
⍝ stimuli that you can receive from your system. They are as follows:
⍝ 
⍝ Input Stimuli:

S←1 ⍝ Set button was pressed
T←2 ⍝ Alarm wire tripped
B←3 ⍝ Bad password digit was pressed
C←4 ⍝ Clear button was pressed
G←5 ⍝ Good password digit was pressed

∇ SPEC

⍝ Here's a beginning sketch for your specification/state machine. 
⍝ Notice that each state is indicated by a starting label (we use _ as a suffix 
⍝ to denote such labels). You then need to call the SYSTEM function with ⎕LC
⍝ to wait to get your next event/stimuli. 
⍝ 
⍝ Your job is to fill out the first state, and then continue filling out each 
⍝ new state that is required to be specified until all transitions branch back 
⍝ to previous states and don't branch to any new sequences. 
⍝ 
⍝ We've sketched out an example of the first two states, where you have seen
⍝ nothing (the first state), and the second state, where you have already seen 
⍝ the S stimuli occur. 

 ∆_: →SYSTEM ⎕LC
 ∆_S: Respones/Events/State changes go here ⋄ →Where to next? 
 ∆_T: ⋄ →
 ∆_B: ⋄ →
 ∆_C: ⋄ →
 ∆_G: ⋄ →
 
 ∆_S_:→SYSTEM ⎕LC
 ∆_S_S: 
 ∆_S_T: 
 ∆_S_B: 
 ∆_S_C: 
 ∆_S_G: 
 
∇

⍝ All the code below has been given to you to help you play with the above 
⍝ specification so that you can see if your system behaves the way you expect. 
⍝ You should not need to touch any of the code below this point. 
⍝ 
⍝ To run and test the system, you can call `SQEN.Run password` with the 3-digit 
⍝ password you want to use to test the system. It will use SPEC to control its 
⍝ behavior. 

sound←8192⍴1○○(⍳100)÷100

∇ Z←SYSTEM lc;opts;res;good_bad;asz
  Z←0
  
  good_bad←{(B G)[password[pidx]=⍵]}
  
  opts←mu.MT_OPT
  opts[mu.(OPT_NOFRAME OPT_NOTITLE OPT_NOCLOSE OPT_NOSCROLL OPT_NORESIZE)]←1
  
 MAIN:→CONT EXIT[(0≠Z)∨⊃res state←mu.do_render struct width height state]
 EXIT:Z←(Z≠0)×Z+lc ⋄ →0
 CONT:mu.begin ⋄ →ALARM_BOX
 
 ALARM_BOX:res←opts mu.begin_window 'Alarm Box' (0 0 width height)
  →CLOSED OPEN[mu.RES_ACTIVE⊃res]
 CLOSED:⎕SIGNAL 99
 OPEN:
  mu.layout_row 3 0
  Z⌈←T×mu.RES_SUBMIT⊃mu.button 'Trip Alarm'
  mu.layout_next mu.draw_rect (light×3⍴255),255
  mu.layout_next mu.draw_rect alarm×255 0 0 255
  Z⌈←S×mu.RES_SUBMIT⊃mu.button 'Set'
  pidx×←0=Z⌈←C×mu.RES_SUBMIT⊃mu.button 'Clear'
  mu.layout_row 3 0
  {Z⌈←(good_bad ⍵)×mu.RES_SUBMIT⊃mu.button (⍕⍵)}¨1+⍳9
  {}mu.layout_next ⋄ Z⌈←(good_bad 0)×mu.RES_SUBMIT⊃mu.button '0'
  mu.end_window ⋄ mu.end
  Z×←light∨Z=S ⋄ pidx+←G=Z ⋄ pidx⌈←(B=Z)×(≢password)-1
  →ALARM
 
 ALARM:→FULL READY[0<asz←fa_avail aptr]
 FULL:→MAIN
 READY:{}fa_write aptr (alarm×asz⍴sound) asz ⋄ →MAIN
∇

∇ {Z}←Run password;width;height;struct;state;pidx;aptr

  'fa_get'⎕NA'P ',fenster,'|fenster_audio_get'
  'fa_open'⎕NA'I ',fenster,'|fenster_audio_open P'
  'fa_avail'⎕NA'I ',fenster,'|fenster_audio_available P'
  'fa_write'⎕NA'',fenster,'|fenster_audio_write P <F4[] U8'
  'fa_close'⎕NA'',fenster,'|fenster_audio_close P'

  width←85×3 ⋄ height←6×33 ⋄ pidx←0 ⋄ password←(3↑password),¯1
  {}fa_open⊢aptr←fa_get
  →0⍴⍨0=⊃struct state←mu.begin_render 'Sequence Enumeration Exercise' width height
  SPEC
  {}fa_close aptr
  mu.end_render struct ⋄ →0
∇

:EndNamespace